{#
    Twelve months of spend that have already happened.

    The forecast card's mirror image, and deliberately the same picture drawn
    by the same code: `SpendChartService::fromHistory()` builds the payload,
    `partials/spend_chart.twig` draws it, and the axis, the peak marker and
    every formatted figure follow the same rules as the year ahead. Two charts
    a reader is meant to compare have to be comparable.

    **These months are reconstructed, not recorded.** The application tracks
    what is due, not a ledger of payments taken, so the past is rebuilt from
    each subscription's start date, its billing cycle and its recorded price
    history — the same walk the Analytics page's year-over-year card is totalled
    from, so the two price a past charge identically, over windows that differ
    at the edges (twelve calendar months here, a rolling year there). A
    subscription with no start date contributes nothing rather than an invented
    amount: under-reporting the past is the right direction to be wrong in.

    One line, not two. The forecast draws a second line for what converting
    trials will add, because that is the one future cost still worth a decision.
    A trial in the past either converted — in which case the charges are here as
    themselves — or cost nothing, so there is nothing to shade.
#}
{% import 'partials/spend_chart.twig' as trend %}

<section class="card chart-card">
    <header class="card-header">
        <h2>{{ t('dashboard.spend_history') }}</h2>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="/stats">{{ t('nav.analytics') }}</a>
    </header>

    {#
        What the heading leaves out: that these figures were rebuilt rather than
        recorded, and which currency they are stated in. Only when there is a
        picture to describe — the message that replaces an undrawable chart is
        already an explanation, and a currency line above it would be claiming a
        total the card has just refused to state.
    #}
    {% if history.is_drawable %}
        <p class="muted">{{ t('dashboard.spend_history_note', {'currency': history.currency}) }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    {{ trend.spend_chart(
        history,
        'dashboard-history-data',
        t('dashboard.spend_history_alt', {'currency': history.currency}),
        t('dashboard.history_part_month_note'),
        t('dashboard.history_unconvertible', {
            'currencies': history.unconvertible|join(', '),
            'currency': history.currency,
        })
    ) }}
</section>
